/*!
\page page_stetofpidtraits StETofPidTraits

\brief Endcap TOF (eTOF) particle identification traits for a matched track.

\section stetofpidtraits_overview Overview

\ref StETofPidTraits stores PID information for a track matched to a hit in the STAR
Endcap Time-of-Flight detector (2.05 < |η| < 2.50, introduced in Run 19).  The eTOF
extends STAR's time-of-flight PID reach to the backward end-cap region.

Compared to \ref StBTofPidTraits, this class adds local-coordinate residuals (ΔX, ΔY)
and uses a 16-bit match flag.  Per-species nσ values were not yet implemented in the
initial version.

\section stetofpidtraits_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code{.txt}
StObject
  └── StTrackPidTraits
           └── StETofPidTraits
\endcode

\section stetofpidtraits_members Key Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| \c mMatchFlag | \c UShort_t | Matching quality flag (0 = unmatched). |
| \c mLocalX / \c mLocalY | \c Float_t | Local coordinates at the counter (cm). |
| \c mDeltaX / \c mDeltaY | \c Float_t | Track–hit residuals (cm). |
| \c mThetaLocal | \c Float_t | Local incident angle (rad). |
| \c mPosition | \c StThreeVectorF | Global extrapolated position (cm). |
| \c mTimeOfFlight | \c Float_t | Measured TOF (ns); −999 if unset. |
| \c mPathLength | \c Float_t | Path length from vertex (cm); −999 if unset. |
| \c mBeta | \c Float_t | β = v/c; −999 if unset. |

\section stetofpidtraits_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
const StETofPidTraits* etof = nullptr;
for (const StTrackPidTraits* p : track->pidTraits()) {
    etof = dynamic_cast<const StETofPidTraits*>(p);
    if (etof) break;
}

if (etof && etof->matchFlag() > 0) {
    double beta = etof->beta();
    double p    = track->geometry()->momentum().mag();
    double m2   = p*p*(1./(beta*beta) - 1.);
}
\endcode

\see StTrackPidTraits
\see StETofCollection
\see StTrack
*/
